print_status prints a formatted status line to stderr: a message followed by a
colored, right-aligned status label, e.g.:

  deployment finished..........................................[ SUCCESS ]

Each status has its own subcommand (success, failure, notice, warning,
unknown) plus common aliases (ok/oke, fail/nok, info, warn, undefined).
Everything after the subcommand name is joined with spaces and used as
the message.
